<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="58306" href="schedule/2011/fall/NRES/285/58306.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2011" href="schedule/2011.xml">2011</calendarYear><term id="120118" href="schedule/2011/fall.xml">Fall 2011</term><subject id="NRES" href="schedule/2011/fall/NRES.xml">Natural Resources and Environmental Sciences</subject><course id="285" href="schedule/2011/fall/NRES/285.xml">Field Experience</course></parents><sectionNumber>WWQ</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Watershed Water Quality</sectionTitle><sectionDateRange>Meets 22-Aug-11 - 14-Oct-11.</sectionDateRange><creditHours>1 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Using the local Salt Fork watershed, students will learn about all aspects of the watershed that affect water quality. We will conduct hands-on field measurements (including stream gaging), understand the sources of pollution (sewage treatment, agriculture), learn about how people view and utilize the watershed, and see how the biology of the stream responds to nutrient and sediment inputs.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Natural Resrcs &amp; Environ Sci major(s). </sectionNotes><sectionFeeAmount>ACES Field Trip $50.00 Flat Fee. </sectionFeeAmount><partOfTerm>A</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2011-08-22Z</startDate><endDate>2011-10-14Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="B1 ">Laboratory</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>W      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>S509</roomNumber><buildingName>Turner Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Czapar" firstName="G">Czapar, G</instructor><instructor lastName="David" firstName="M">David, M</instructor></instructors></meeting><meeting id="1"><type code="LEC">Lecture</type><start>01:00 PM</start><end>01:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>W      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>N107</roomNumber><b